wick-county"],["ARC or PLC in Sedgwick County","/arc-plc/kansas/sedgwick-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on Sedgwick County runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids. January to February and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 39 years, the most of any pair. In 2025, February to March came in at 24% of normal on the middle, and June to July hit 192%. For grid 21130, the preliminary estimate for July to August 2026 is 22.7.</p>"}
